/**
@mainpage snesrecomp Runtime SDK

@tableofcontents

The runtime SDK is the portable C boundary between a recompiled SNES game,
the hardware runner, optional enhancement code, and the host frontend. This
reference is generated from the installed headers, so declarations and their
ownership rules stay beside the code they describe.

Start with these documents:

- @ref api_reference "API usage, capabilities, ownership, and call sequences"
- @ref game_enhancement_integration "Integrating widescreen graphics and enhanced audio"
- @ref runtime_architecture "Runtime, game, and host boundaries"

Most external enhancement and tooling code should acquire SnesRunnerApi with
sr_runner_get_api(), verify the required capability and table extent, and use
only opaque SrRunnerHandle values. The linked game module uses RtlGameModule
plus the deliberately smaller synchronous helpers in game_runtime.h.

Nothing under `src/` is an SDK contract. The headers under
`snesrecomp/game/` support generated C and are intentionally omitted from this
human integration index; they remain installed and compile-tested.
*/

/** @defgroup sr_runner Runner ABI
 *  @brief Versioned, capability-gated inspection and enhancement services.
 *
 *  This is the normal surface for host code, tools, and optional enhancement
 *  layers. Calls are synchronous unless a contract explicitly describes a
 *  queued safe-point mutation.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_core Core runner state
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Results, handles, generations, borrowed memory, CPU state, timing,
 *  and input state.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_ppu PPU and presentation
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Coherent PPU snapshots, widescreen policy, captures, rendering,
 *  and scanout transactions.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_events Events and diagnostics
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Execution, memory, DMA, interrupt, frame, and audio observation.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_audio Audio control
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Bounded SPC handshakes and native DSP bus-mix policy.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_mutation Safe-point mutation
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Copied commands queued from host threads and applied at frame-safe
 *  boundaries.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_runner_table API discovery and dispatch
 *  @ingroup sr_runner
 *  @brief Runtime descriptor, ABI discovery, and the SnesRunnerApi table.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_game Linked game module
 *  @brief Contracts implemented by a recompiled game and registered before
 *  runner creation.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_game_hotpath Linked-game hot path
 *  @ingroup sr_game
 *  @brief Low-overhead synchronous helpers reserved for the game linked into
 *  the runner executable.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_game_audio Linked-game audio adaptation
 *  @ingroup sr_game
 *  @brief Safe-point audio routing, SPC upload, extension, and save-state
 *  contracts implemented by game-aware adapters.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_host Host conveniences
 *  @brief Optional portable ROM loading and launch-path helpers.
 */

/** @defgroup sr_support Stateless support
 *  @brief Small portable helpers with no runner ownership or lifecycle.
 */
